WEBVTT

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:36.640
No!

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:38.640
This is...

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.640
It's too much!

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:43.140
Why aren't you here for me?

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:44.780
Ash!

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:52.080
Let us end this once and for all,

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.780
daughter of Avalon.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:12.300
A dream?

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:47.080
Why are you up so early?

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:53.090
Uh, i-it's just... my bed... I...

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:58.090
You mean...

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:01.600
<i>Fafnirite? The dragon discharge?</i>

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:03.180
Lemme see!

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.060
No way!

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.360
It's too embarrassing!

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:07.600
Embarrassing?

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.230
Well, obviously.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:14.100
It's okay. I promise I won't laugh.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.110
I accept you just the way you are.

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:19.360
Really?

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:21.370
Yep!

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:24.370
All right.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:29.670
Huh?

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:33.250
You... wet the bed?!

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:38.960
What did you think it was?!

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.890
I figured it'd be Fafnirite.

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:46.390
That would be even
<i>more</i> embarrassing!

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.520
Seriously?

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.320
Between the Zepharos Empire to the north

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:04.540
and the Chevron Kingdom to the south

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:06.460
lies Lautreamont Knight Country.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:08.600
Known as "Dragon-Rearing Land,"

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:13.070
it boasts the largest dragon population on the Arc Strada continent.

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:19.610
This small country with fewer than five million citizens is home to a unique school:

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:21.500
Ansullivan Dragonar Academy.

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.090
It aims to educate and guide dragon masters

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:27.200
and the so-called Breeders,
those young men and women

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.000
who have entered into bonds with dragons.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:37.100
Meeting you smack in the middle of the world
sekai no domannaka de kimi to deatte

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:42.360
Leaves me breathless
kokyuu mo dekinai kurai ni natte

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:46.740
The “something" between you and me
chiisaku tokuntokun to hajimaru

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:49.860
Starts with small heartbeats
kimi to boku no nanika

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:53.540
Now teach me about the sky one more time
saa mou ikkai sora wo oshiete

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:57.370
Seikoku no Dragonar

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:02.380
Only birds know how heavy their flapping wings are
tori dake ga shiru habataku hane no omosa

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:07.380
Everyone longs for wings without knowing it
minna wa nani mo shirazu ni akogareteru

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:14.680
You smiled with a slightly sorrowful look
kimi wa chotto setsunai kao de waratta

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:17.850
I... I have nothing
boku ni wa ne nani mo nai

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:20.520
But if it makes you shed less tears
demo kimi no namida ga hette

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:23.020
And smile like you mean it
honki no kao de warau nara

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:25.570
Then be it a hero or anything else
hero datte donnan datte

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:28.030
I'll become whatever you ask of me
narikitte yaru kara sa

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:32.280
I'll never, never, never, never let go
zettai zettai zettai zettai hanasanai

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:37.290
Even if I die, I'll be your knight
shindemo kimi dake no naito de iru

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:41.670
But you cried for real and got angry
demo honki de naite kimi wa okotta

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.540
You said, “Don't be so cold to me"
tsumetaku nante sasenai

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:47.540
I wipe your tears
to boku wa namida wo fuku

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:50.050
I don't need a sacred blade
seiken nante nakutatte ii

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:53.300
I don't care if I'm not a hero
yuusha ja nakutatte kamawanai

00:04:53.300 --> 00:05:01.100
As long as I can protect you all the way
kimi hitori wo mamorikireru naraba

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:05.950
Lucca Sarlinen

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.700
Honestly!

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:12.700
Three employees up
and quit, at a time like this?

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:14.710
This is our high season.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:17.990
And all three are quitting
to get married too.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:19.810
This is no laughing matter!

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.310
And the icing on the cake?

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:24.130
"You should find yourself
a man too, Miss!"

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:25.970
The nerve!

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.590
Well, Princess Veronica
is single! And me?

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:32.030
My work is my life!

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:35.560
So, uh...

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.830
Oh, right, the interview!

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:41.440
Yes, yes, you're hired!

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:45.450
Thank you so much! I'll do
my very best in the kitchen.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:47.950
In the kitchen?

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.840
It'd be a waste to keep you
behind the scenes.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:53.450
Pardon?

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.550
You'll be working as a waitress!

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:57.710
Huh?!

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.510
What? Eco's taking the day off?

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:05.870
Yeah, she's pretty cranky.

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:11.470
We'll need a lot more interactions if we're gonna mend the rift between humans and dragonkind.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:14.610
It's already Gemini. Almost time for camp.

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:18.980
Are they announcing the
attendees at today's assembly?

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:24.110
Most of the glorious Order of the Sacred Dragonars of Lautreamont went to this training camp.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:26.810
It's like a gateway to the elite track.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:30.810
Well, it has nothing to do with us.

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:31.990
Yeah.

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:36.000
First-year Senios Jupito Dion!

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.030
Here!

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:39.650
First-year Senios Alis Vargan!

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:40.000
Here!

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:43.000
Please approach the stage.

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:47.530
And though she's absent today, our final camp attendee is...

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:50.510
third-year Junios Lucca Sarlinen.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:52.090
Playing hooky <i>again</i>?

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.640
I guess that's how you get picked for camp.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.510
What a crock!

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:58.520
Wow. Why all the backlash?

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:02.520
Well, she hasn't been to class
in nearly three months.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.800
Who is this... Lucca, was it?

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:09.150
How can you not know <i>her</i>?
She's the Student Council secretary.

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:13.030
Maybe so, but I've never met her.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:15.040
Lucca Sarlinen.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:19.050
She's so talented that she's the youngest person ever chosen as a Dragonar.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:21.790
She even beat Rebecca's record.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:24.990
Rebecca's?! That's amazing.

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:26.350
Silence.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:30.300
These, then, are our
training camp attendees.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:33.390
Like I said, nothing to do with us.

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:34.050
Yep.

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:39.060
And finally, we have a student
attending by special invitation.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.560
Special invitation?

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:47.340
This year, we have created a new category for those students not selected to attend.

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:50.790
Now for the head of the
selection committee, Rebecca.

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:51.590
Yes, sir.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:58.200
I have chosen one student to attend by special invitation:

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:01.210
first-year Senios Ash Blake!

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:09.950
Huh?!

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.850
Why did you choose me?

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:19.600
Because you've been given
a unique Pal in Eco.

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:25.860
Because you defeated the Necromancia and drove out Avdocha, She Who Condemns.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.940
You definitely have talent.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.940
I-I see...

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:34.680
But under the old selection criteria,

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.830
there's no way you
would've made the cut.

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:39.450
Accordingly, I came up with
a whole new category,

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:43.210
just so you could attend training camp.

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:46.490
All that, just for me?

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:51.090
Yes. Just for you.

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:54.090
I want to develop that talent of yours.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:56.790
Can I expect great things from you?

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:59.180
U-Um...

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:00.110
Miss President!

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:07.230
Eavesdropping is most unbecoming.

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:12.150
Miss President!
It's an emergency!

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:15.530
A fire?

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:16.060
Where?

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:18.230
Isn't that the Ecbladian's room?

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:28.360
A-A coffin?!

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:30.150
No way!

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:32.270
I-Is she dead?

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:40.730
Oh no! What are we gonna do?
This is terrible!

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:43.070
What should we do?

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:02.190
So all that smoke was
from the incense?

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:07.960
I'm sorry for the
trouble I've caused.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:11.250
No problem. At least
you're all right.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.460
Just be careful not to
burn too much at once.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:16.720
You're always right.

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:19.670
So yes, I will be careful.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:23.560
There's trouble, and then
there's <i>trouble</i>.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:25.980
I mean, what's with the coffin?

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:28.350
It's not a coffin.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:30.480
It's an Ecbladian bed.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.980
A versatile bed you can
also use at your funeral.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:36.490
So it <i>is</i> a coffin!

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:40.990
Lucca's sensitive.
Don't be too hard on her.

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:45.490
Lucca? So she's the Junios who got picked for training camp?

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:50.750
This is the first time you Student Council newbies have met her.

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:55.570
Lucca Sarlinen is an Ecbladian,
a fairy of the forest.

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:59.450
Her people have a knack
for herbal medicine,

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:01.760
and their potions are
highly valued the world over.

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:08.270
The Ecbladians are also a warrior clan, with many Dragonars among them.

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:11.770
Of course, Lucca's skill is no secret.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:14.270
She broke my record

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:18.030
for being the youngest
Dragonar in history.

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:24.570
By the way, Lucca, how are things with your Pal, Gawain?

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:28.290
Not good.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:31.130
Any idea what the problem is?

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:32.290
No.

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:35.790
It's not that I can't ride him anymore.

00:11:36.390 --> 00:11:40.300
Gawain won't <i>let</i> me ride him.

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:47.530
So it's been three months since Lucca last rode Gawain.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:52.440
We can't do much to help if we don't know why he won't let her ride.

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:55.020
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:12:03.120
The problem lies in an interruption of
the astral flow that connects Lucca and Gawain.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:07.030
If this goes on much longer,
Gawain's life will be in danger.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.410
So there!

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.250
Smells like sunshine!

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:21.310
Let us end this once and for all,

00:12:21.310 --> 00:12:24.180
daughter of Avalon.

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:35.950
<i>Dragons draw life force from humans through the astral flow.</i>

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:40.030
<i>If that's been interrupted for
three months now...</i>

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:48.040
Seikoku no Dragonar
Seikoku no Dragonar

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:52.040
Seikoku no Dragonar
Seikoku no Dragonar

00:12:57.400 --> 00:13:00.460
It has been two weeks since
I infiltrated the school eatery.

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:02.550
I'll investigate this place thoroughly

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:04.860
and find their weakness!

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:07.300
They'd better prepare themselves!

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:22.510
Ow...

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:25.990
Why did he come to mind?

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:43.370
Anya?

00:13:43.370 --> 00:13:45.350
C-Coming!

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:49.010
Huh?

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:52.010
Your help is needed
at the training camp?

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:55.480
I can't very well
close this place down.

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:58.840
Why don't you let me run it, then?

00:13:58.840 --> 00:13:59.610
What?

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:02.230
Oh, pretty please?

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:06.960
I'm coming in, Eco.

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:14.750
Wh-What was that for?

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:16.490
You're late!

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:25.010
Hey, slow down, okay?

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:27.590
What's wrong?

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:37.480
Are you all right?

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:39.850
Eco?

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:43.230
I had a nightmare.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:45.730
A nightmare?

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:51.000
And the bad guy in my dream looked like the Necromancia,

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:52.610
but it wasn't.

00:14:52.610 --> 00:14:54.490
He had nine eyes, for one thing.

00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:58.490
He was super-huge and totally bizarre.

00:14:58.490 --> 00:15:01.050
Just, like, absolutely evil.

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:04.130
And though I shouldn't have
known this... this <i>thing</i>,

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:08.130
it felt like we'd met lots of times before, way back then.

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:26.570
Scoot over.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:28.150
Wh-What?

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:29.900
What's going on?

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:35.160
This is what we did when I was little and too scared to sleep.

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:37.910
Ash...

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:39.920
And if we sleep together like this,

00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:41.920
you probably won't
wet the bed again, either.

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:47.940
Do you seriously think I'd commit such an indignity again?

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:50.920
N-No! I meant no offense, honestly!

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:54.680
Well, you'd better quit it!

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:04.190
Does this mean...
you're feeling better?

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:15.730
Why are dragons seen in a different light? Why do we consider them sacred?

00:16:15.730 --> 00:16:17.610
The old Eco is back, I see.

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:18.110
There are many reasons, to be sure,

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:19.590
Yep, sleeping like a baby.

00:16:19.590 --> 00:16:21.130
but chief among them is their capacity for magic.

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:23.820
So you fixed that human-dragon rift you were talking about.

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:25.150
Now, then...

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:27.210
So you fixed that human-dragon rift you were talking about.

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:31.210
Trust me, we still have
a long way to go.

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:31.970
Ow, my back.

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:33.950
A long way to go?

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:37.710
All those late-night "discussions"...

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:40.730
Whatever you're picturing,
it didn't happen.

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:44.980
I wonder what Eco's like at night.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:47.480
Probably all "No, don't."

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:49.310
Lucca?

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:02.500
Gawain.

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:34.630
Lucca.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:41.410
Rebecca, how can we get Lucca and Gawain back the way they were?

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:43.660
Well, this is rather sudden.

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:46.890
I didn't see my Pal
for the longest time,

00:17:46.890 --> 00:17:48.590
and then I met Eco.

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:52.670
I can relate to how
Lucca must be feeling.

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.420
Therefore, I can't just
leave her like that.

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:57.830
I want to help her!

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:03.230
There <i>is</i> a way, but...

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:04.680
Please tell me!

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:08.130
It could be very dangerous.

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.190
You must ride Gawain.

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:12.090
Huh?

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:15.450
When you rode the Necromancia,

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:17.950
it looked like you could
sense its intentions.

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:21.700
Well, yes, vaguely.

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:25.200
I want you to try the
same thing with Gawain.

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:27.250
All right. I will.

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:28.710
But first...

00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:35.210
Lucca, can you try communicating with Gawain again?

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:38.520
Hm, maybe not "communicate."

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:42.230
Try talking with Gawain again.

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:43.480
Is that better?

00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:46.190
What are you mumbling
about? Let's go!

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:47.980
I'm still psyching myself up.

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:49.100
Hey!

00:18:53.930 --> 00:18:55.080
Stop that.

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.050
It'll melt.

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:03.150
Quit staring!

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:12.630
Lucca, we need to talk. It's serious.

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:16.920
How cute!

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:19.420
Those horns!

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:21.350
Gimme!

00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:26.550
Can I have them, please?

00:19:26.550 --> 00:19:28.550
Of course you can't!

00:19:28.550 --> 00:19:30.640
Then can I taste them?

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:35.270
No! Not my horns!

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:39.870
I belong to the proud dragon race!

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:41.150
Wh-What are you...

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:42.280
I'll c-crush...

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:46.630
N-No, please... please, stop!

00:19:53.490 --> 00:19:54.670
Cut that out.

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:59.740
Well, I guess I'll go back to sleep.

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:02.970
Lucca, listen to me.

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:06.010
Rebecca's waiting
at Dragon Pen 7.

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:09.890
What are you going to
do to Gawain?

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:12.880
Don't worry. We're not
doing anything.

00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:15.400
This is for you and Gawain.

00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:19.650
All right. I'll get ready.

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:25.870
Why are you undressing?!

00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:31.830
I'm changing to go meet Gawain.

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:36.630
I'm glad you came, Lucca.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:39.730
Ash is about to ride Gawain.

00:20:39.730 --> 00:20:42.130
That way, we can ask why
he's rejecting you.

00:20:43.170 --> 00:20:46.640
But first, could you try talking with Gawain one more time?

00:20:47.110 --> 00:20:49.900
That'd be the best
way to resolve this.

00:20:58.720 --> 00:20:59.990
Gawain?

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:23.970
You're giving up already?!

00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:28.570
It's just...

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:31.970
not working!

00:21:35.800 --> 00:21:37.070
Let's begin.

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:42.250
<i>Bujeta, hombrera, brazal, guarda, escarpe!</i>

00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:45.030
<i>Espolazo!</i>

00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:53.500
Oh! Sir Silver Knight!

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:55.650
Just don't do anything rash.

00:21:55.650 --> 00:21:56.650
I won't.

00:21:57.570 --> 00:21:59.500
Thanks, Eco.

00:21:59.970 --> 00:22:03.760
Save your words.
Thank me with crepes.

00:22:04.230 --> 00:22:06.170
We're counting on you, Ash.

00:22:18.140 --> 00:22:21.870
<i>Gawain, why are you
rejecting Lucca?</i>

00:22:21.870 --> 00:22:25.150
<i>Tell me how you feel!</i>

00:22:33.100 --> 00:22:34.130
Gawain?

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:36.160
Ash! Above you!

00:22:44.180 --> 00:22:46.430
Ash!

00:24:19.640 --> 00:24:20.310
Ash?

00:24:20.310 --> 00:24:21.020
What's up, Lucca?

00:24:21.020 --> 00:24:23.130
Do you hate girls who
don't wear underpants?

00:24:23.130 --> 00:24:24.230
That's pretty random!

00:24:24.230 --> 00:24:26.440
So you <i>do</i> hate me.

00:24:26.440 --> 00:24:27.730
I didn't say that!

00:24:27.740 --> 00:24:28.570
Then you love me?

00:24:28.570 --> 00:24:30.710
Well, uh, I don't... hate you?

00:24:30.710 --> 00:24:31.370
You're nasty.

00:24:31.370 --> 00:24:34.030
Geez, put me between
a rock and a hard place!
